okf_version: "1.0"
task: "CielAiRouter direct gateway data path (opt-in gateway_data_path=router|direct): the CLI talks to the selected gateway itself; the local router stays the control plane."
reported: >
  Approved plan C:/Users/djlov/.claude/plans/temporal-enchanting-newt.md (2026-10-16): remove the Runtime HTTP hop in
  CLI -> Ciel router -> CielAiRouter gateway -> provider for CielAiRouter only, while Ciel Runtime keeps SSE event
  receipt, session injection, MCP and restart control. Other providers unchanged. Default stays router.
design:
  capability:
    - "architecture.py ProviderConfigurationPolicy.supports_gateway_data_path (False) and launch_gateway(config, log) -> None; ProviderOptionPresentationPolicy.show_gateway_data_path (False)."
    - "providers/cielairouter.py: CielAiRouterConfigurationPolicy returns True and delegates launch_gateway to cielairouter_gateway_overlay.select_launch_gateway; CielAiRouterPresentationPolicy.show_gateway_data_path True. No provider-name branch was added to generic launch code."
  selection:
    - "cielairouter_gateway_overlay.select_launch_gateway(pcfg): same _load_selector (CielAiRouterGatewayService), select(central, first transportable key, current_model, fresh=True). Healthy, non-degraded, non-central result -> LaunchGateway(endpoint, node, reason, central origin, upstream model = forced_model or current_model without [1m], key). Otherwise endpoint empty + reason. No new discovery code."
    - "launch_data_path.LaunchDataPathResolver (provider-neutral): configured router -> no selection, no log, no output; configured direct -> policy.launch_gateway; active=direct only for HTTPS or loopback HTTP with key and model. Every other case active=router with one WARN line 'launch_data_path ... active=router reason=...'. Record <workspace state>/launch-data-path.json per CLI (no key). api_key is repr=False and never in records/text."
  claude_code:
    - "runtime_launch.run_claude: resolve only when use_router_mode; direct -> env_vars(cfg, data_path=route) (ClaudeEnvironmentProjection.build): ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL = gateway root, ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN = router key, ANTHROPIC_MODEL / DEFAULT_HAIKU|OPUS|SONNET / CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL / CIEL_RUNTIME_MODEL_ALIAS (also --model) = resolve_requested_model upstream ids; ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_MODEL_OPTION follows. Router mode calls env_vars(cfg) exactly as before."
    - "Restart: a launch that started direct selects again; no healthy gateway -> ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL/AUTH_TOKEN back to the router values (router accepts upstream ids). A launch that fell back to router stays router until relaunch."
  codex:
    - "Plain TUI (run_codex) and app-server/codex-remote (run_codex_app_server), router codex_mode only: codex_runtime_config_args(gateway_root, env_key=CIEL_RUNTIME_GATEWAY_API_KEY) -> model_providers.ciel-runtime.base_url=<gateway>/v1, env_key names the secret env; env CIEL_RUNTIME_GATEWAY_API_KEY = router key; -m / -c model = upstream id; model catalog slug = upstream id (runtime_model_catalog_args(model_slug=...)). Provider block id unchanged. codex-remote TUI inherits the server -c overrides."
    - "Restart (run_codex loop, codex-remote relaunch): select again; provider-block base_url/env_key rewritten (launch_data_path.codex_provider_command); no gateway -> router /v1 + CIEL_RUNTIME_CODEX_API_KEY local key."
  unchanged_in_direct: "Router start (start_router_if_needed), router MCP (/ca/mcp) args, workspace MCP, channel proxy and session socket, external SSE receiver, session restart supervision, authenticated_codex_command."
  wiring: "ClaudeLaunchConfig.launch_data_path / ClaudeLaunchConfigPorts.data_path (10 fields), CodexLaunchServices.data_path and CodexAppServerLaunchServices.data_path (10), CodexLaunchAssembly.data_path (9). Facade: launch_data_resolver() one-liner; env_vars(cfg, data_path); ciel_runtime.py 4980 lines (budget 4980)."
  ui: "provider-options cielairouter gateway_data_path=router|direct|unset; set_llm_option_config key gateway_data_path (prelaunch LLM options row 'Gateway data path', Enter toggles); external menu choices gateway_data_path=router/direct; provider status shows gateway_data_path=...; gateway-status appends configured path, live re-route note and per-CLI last launch path. Other providers: 'gateway_data_path is only available for cielairouter' (SystemExit)."
verification:
  unit: "tests/test_launch_data_path.py 36 OK: router default parity (env equal, launch cmd/env equal with and without resolver, no selection, no output), direct env/args for Claude, Codex TUI, app-server + remote TUI, every fallback (selection off, discovery failure, degraded, central, remote http, credentials in URL, no key, no model, selector exception, non-gateway result), other providers isolated (anthropic, openrouter, opencode, vllm, deepseek, codex), key absent from argv/logs/output/record/status/repr, router MCP + messaging socket + router start kept in direct, restart reselect and router fallback, real CielAiRouterGatewayService with injected discovery/probe, option CLI/panel/menu/status."
  focused_suites: "49 related files, 1273 tests OK (skipped=55) in isolated state with CIEL_RUNTIME_* unset; contracts (test_architecture_contracts, test_provider_contract_matrix, test_architecture_budget) included. evidence/focused-tests.txt"
  local_http_stub: "evidence/stub_selection.py/.out: loopback central + gateway stubs. Discovery carried the router key as Bearer; /healthz carried no Authorization; the remote plain-http node was never probed; route active=direct to the stub gateway; Claude env aliases -> upstream ids; Codex provider block -> <gateway>/v1 + CIEL_RUNTIME_GATEWAY_API_KEY; key absent from logs/output/record/repr/argv/status."
  cli: "evidence/cli_option.out: isolated CIEL_RUNTIME_CONFIG_DIR; set direct, gateway-status text incl. live re-route note, vllm rejected (exit 1), invalid value rejected (exit 1), workspace config.json holds gateway_data_path=direct."
  live_router: "127.0.0.1:9512 pid 31392 v0.2.51 before and after every run."
real_cli_e2e_2026_10_16:
  environment: "Windows 11 Enterprise 10.0.26200; source checkout; isolated G:/ciel-e2e/direct-path run directories; child launch batch explicitly cleared inherited CIEL_RUNTIME_*, ANTHROPIC_*, CLAUDE_*, CODEX_* and OPENAI_* variables; live router 127.0.0.1:9512 pid 31392 v0.2.51 remained healthy before and after."
  versions: "Claude Code 2.1.302; Codex CLI 0.163.0; Python 3.11.6."
  claude: "PASS. Real Claude Code received direct Anthropic Messages requests at gateway A (/v1/messages) and after restart at B; central saw zero generation POSTs; local router log had zero POST /v1/messages, /v1/responses or /v1/chat/completions. External receiver SSE connected, two synthetic 951-character bodies were injected exactly head-to-tail and reached A then B. MCP restart_session returned queued=true; launch_data_path selected A then B; restart notice reached B."
  codex_remote: "PASS. Real Codex remote TUI 0.163.0 sent direct Responses requests at gateway A then B; central saw zero generation POSTs; local router had zero model POSTs. The two synthetic SSE bodies matched exactly in the Codex transcript and reached A then B; app-server restart selected B and completed restart notice/event turns."
  plain_codex: "PASS for guard. Real plain Codex TUI did not use direct mode: launch log says active=router with reason that whole-message channel delivery requires router model HTTP. Its synthetic SSE body appeared as router [ciel-wake] marker transport, and router POST /v1/responses was observed. The plain flow was not used as direct gateway proof (by design)."
  gateway_observations: "Discovery requests carried the synthetic key (recorded only as bearer-router-key); /healthz probes carried no Authorization; gateway model rows used stub-model. No key or request body is stored in the fact bundles."
  screenshots: "Three nonblank PNG PrintWindow captures per direct flow at evidence/e2e/run-claude/shots and evidence/e2e/run-codex-remote/shots, 1129x635, with saved hashes in transcript-facts.json."
  evidence: "evidence/e2e/run-claude/e2e-facts.json, whole-body-facts.json, transcript-facts.json; corresponding run-codex-remote files; run-codex/plain-fallback-facts.json."
  limitation: "Claude channel logs also recorded the isolated session-socket auth_key_unavailable fallback and prompt_not_submitted statuses, while the actual event bodies were nevertheless present exactly in the Claude transcript and direct gateway requests. This is an existing isolated E2E transport observation, not a direct gateway HTTP failure."

not_done:
  - "Earlier real-CLI E2E gap is now closed for Claude and codex-remote; see real_cli_e2e_2026_10_16. Live gateway-fleet compatibility remains unverified (only local synthetic gateways used)."
  - "Full 4-group suite not run (parent runs it)."
limits:
  - "Direct requests skip router request handling: key rotation, provider failover, per-request gateway failure cooldown/reselection, catalog output caps and effort lowering. A gateway failing mid-session fails that CLI's requests until restart."
  - "Channel deliveries that rely on the router appending the body to a '[ciel-wake] pending_ids=...' marker (router transport) cannot get the body in direct mode (code reading: channel_message_prompt.format_llm_delivery_wake_prompt docstring, runtime_launch Codex wake comment). Claude session-socket delivery and codex-remote app-server injection send the whole message. Plain Codex TUI on Windows types only the marker, so its channel delivery is expected to lose the body in direct mode; unverified until E2E."
  - "[1m] is not sent to the gateway; Claude Code's context still comes from CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS. Whether the gateway accepts every Claude Code request shape (count_tokens, betas) directly is unverified until E2E."
  - "An explicit --model on the command line goes to the gateway as given."

revision_2026_10_16_seam_review:
  supersedes: "Earlier plain-Codex-direct and lost-body limitations above are superseded by this revision."
  plain_codex: "Configured direct explicitly falls back to router with reason: plain Codex TUI needs router model HTTP for whole-message channel delivery. No gateway discovery occurs."
  whole_message_delivery: "Launch-scoped parent environment CIEL_RUNTIME_DIRECT_GATEWAY_ACTIVE: channel_pending_injection reroutes explicit router/default/session_socket messages to whole-message socket, or full TTY body if no socket; codex_desktop_injection uses RPC rather than router deferral."
  restart: "Claude rebuilds env/model/capabilities and generated --model before relaunch. App-server rebuilds provider/model/catalog/effort snapshot, retaining MCP/listen/session arguments. Plain Codex stays router."
  identity: "Facade injects existing resolve_requested_model into LaunchDataPathResolver; unresolved ciel-runtime aliases fail closed to router. Direct Codex provider id ciel-runtime-gateway is distinct from local router; env key CIEL_RUNTIME_GATEWAY_API_KEY."
  observations: "Request-level TUI model-response observation does not exist in direct mode; transcript agent.turn_ended survives. Status/docs explicitly state this."
  verification: "582 focused tests OK (54 skipped), including updated launch tests, whole socket/TTY delivery and busy app-server router-transport RPC tests, architecture contracts/budget/provider matrix, restart, Codex config/runtime, overlay and menu tests. Earlier 1273-suite result precedes this review revision. ruff all checks passed; diff check clean; facade 4980 lines."
